# Infra

## Docker

- Lean images. Only what runtime needs — no dev deps, no test fixtures.
- Frozen lockfile in CI builds.
- Volume names must coexist across services without collision.
- Test: build image locally before pushing.

## Kubernetes

- Resource requests/limits reflect measured peaks + margin. Not guesses.
- Ingress: only public-facing services exposed. Internal = cluster-only.
- Port-forward testing: verify via actual HTTP calls, not assumptions.

## Secrets

- Never commit API keys, private keys, `.env` files.
- Server-side secrets stay server-side. Never in client bundles or public env vars.
- Hide sensitive values from build output and console logs.

## CI/CD

- Submodule checkout: recursive, correct depth, access tokens where needed.
- Version bump to trigger image rebuild when CI/CD is image-based.

## Data Safety

- DB migrations: no data loss on live unless explicitly told to nuke.
- Migration state consistency: verify schema matches expectations before and after.
- Staging: manual repair acceptable when ORM state drifts from reality.
